🗃️ Kafka vs RabbitMQ (Quick Summary)
| Feature         | Kafka                                      | RabbitMQ                                      |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |
| Storage model   | Append-only log (durable by design)        | Queue-based (can also be durable if configured)|
| Replay Events   | ✅ Easy (retain + rewind offsets)          | ❌ Not natural (unless you build it)           |
| Throughput      | Very high (often millions/sec class)       | Usually lower than Kafka                      |
| Ordering        | Per-partition                              | Per-queue                                     |
| Consumer model  | Pull + consumer groups                     | Push to consumers / competing consumers       |
| Best for        | Stream processing, event log, analytics    | Background jobs, RPC-style, complex routing   |
| Scalability     | Horizontal via partitions                  | Clustering / quorum queues (different model)  |


