🔄 Kafka Partitioning (Recap)
Topics are split into partitions.
Messages within a partition are ordered.
Consumers in the same group share partitions.

Topic: payments-events
Partitions: 3
Consumers: C1, C2, C3 (same group)
→ Parallel processing of events

If a 4th consumer joins the same group → it stays idle (no free partition).


🔁 Rebalance & Consumer Lag (Know these terms)

Rebalance:
When consumers join/leave a group (or subscriptions change), Kafka reassigns partitions
so work is evenly shared again.
During rebalance, consumption can briefly pause.

How rebalance works (simple):

1) Trigger happens
   - Consumer joins the group
   - Consumer leaves / crashes / times out (misses heartbeat)
   - Topic partitions are added
   - Consumer unsubscribes / changes topics

2) Group Coordinator (a Kafka broker for that group) notices membership change

3) All consumers in the group join a new generation (rebalance starts)
   - Consumers briefly stop fetching / commit offsets for owned partitions
   - Old partition ownership is revoked

4) Assignment strategy decides new mapping
   (e.g. Range, RoundRobin, Sticky, Cooperative Sticky)
   Example strategy goal: give each active consumer some partitions

5) Each consumer gets its new partition list and resumes from committed offsets
   (offsets stay in __consumer_offsets; only ownership moves)

Example:

Before (topic has 3 partitions, group has 2 consumers):
C1 → P0, P1
C2 → P2

Then C3 joins same group → REBALANCE

After:
C1 → P0
C2 → P1
C3 → P2

If C2 crashes:
C1 → P0, P1
C3 → P2
(or similar redistribution)

Important interview points:
- Rebalance = reassign partitions among consumers in ONE group
- Offsets are NOT reset; new owner continues from last committed offset
- Too many rebalances (frequent restarts / long processing without heartbeat) hurt throughput
- Sticky / Cooperative Sticky assignment reduces how many partitions move (less disruption)

Consumer Lag:
How far behind the latest offset a consumer group is.
High lag = consumers too slow / under-scaled / stuck.


